# Portfolio-Lab Crontab — dual-mode (Hermes + system cron) as of 2026-06-08
# Hermes is the scheduler source-of-truth for overlapping jobs.
# System cron is disabled for jobs that Hermes owns.
# System cron remains active for jobs that Hermes does NOT own (unified-dashboard,
# overlay-signals, overlay-dashboard, attribution, daily-pnl, garch-risk).
#
# To fully switch TO system cron (emergency fallback):
#   1. hermes cron pause <job_id>  (for each portfolio-lab job)
#   2. crontab /root/projects/portfolio-lab/crontab
#
# To switch back to Hermes:
#   1. crontab -r
#   2. hermes cron resume <job_id>  (for each portfolio-lab job)
#
# All jobs call the Makefile, which updates data/cron_status.json
# for the dashboard health panel.

# Data pipeline — hourly at :05 (DISABLED: owned by Hermes portfolio-lab-data)
# 5 * * * * export PATH="$HOME/.bun/bin:$PATH" && CRON_BACKEND=crontab make -C /root/projects/portfolio-lab data >> /root/projects/portfolio-lab/data/cron.log 2>&1

